<p>Israel’s parliament approved the country’s defense-heavy 2026 budget early on March 30, passing it 62-55 and averting the automatic collapse of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s government. Under Israeli law, failing to pass a budget by the end of March would have triggered a snap election. The new spending plan arrives as Israel remains at war with Iran, is fighting Hezbollah in Lebanon, and continues operations in Gaza. The vote gives the government breathing room at a moment of regional conflict and locks in higher wartime spending for 2026.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Defense increase: SCMP reported that the budget adds about US$10 billion to Israel’s military spending.</li><li>Weekly cost: Reuters, as cited by Al-Monitor, said the war is costing Israel’s economy about $1.6 billion a week.</li><li>US role: Al-Monitor, citing Reuters, described the Iran conflict as a joint war with the United States, underscoring the broader alliance behind the budget vote.</li><li>War timing: Reuters, as cited by Al-Monitor, said parliament approved the budget about a month into the war with Iran.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>SCMP framing: The wartime spending shift was large enough that the paper described the proposed 2026 total expenditure budget at roughly 850 billion shekels, along with a major defense increase. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3348339/israel-adds-us10-billion-its-war-chest-defence-budget-increase'>SCMP</a>)</li><li>DW framing: The budget passed while Israel was simultaneously fighting Iran, Hezbollah, and conducting operations in Gaza, tying fiscal policy directly to a multi-front military campaign. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-israel-approves-billions-in-new-military-funds/live-76586932'>DW</a>)</li><li>Reuters/Al-Monitor: Reuters’ framing in Al-Monitor emphasized the economic burden, saying the conflict is costing Israel about $1.6 billion a week as the war enters another month. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/israeli-parliament-approves-2026-state-budget-spokesperson-says'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3348339/israel-adds-us10-billion-its-war-chest-defence-budget-increase'>Israel adds US$10 billion to its war chest with defence budget increase</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-israel-approves-billions-in-new-military-funds/live-76586932'>Iran war: Israel approves billions in new military funds</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/israeli-parliament-approves-2026-state-budget-spokesperson-says'>Israeli parliament approves 2026 state budget, spokesperson says</a> - al-monitor.com</li></ul>